=== static members need their type's name, as Kotlin's static-access-good-and-bad
class C {
  private static ap: Int = 1;
  public static a: Int = ap + C.ap;
  public static f(i: Int): Int { i + a + C.a }
  public h(i: Int): Int { 2 * f(i) * C.f(i) }
}
console.log("${C.f(1)} ${new C().h(1)} ${C.a}");
--- settled
(Block
  (Class
    ^C:0
    (Let private static ^ap:2 Int 1)
    (Let static ^a:3 Int (Call + ap:2 (Call . C:0 \ap)))
    (Method static
