=== a setter without a getter is assigned, also as a value, as Kotlin's nested-setter-invocations-in-result-position
class C {
  public set p(newValue: Int) {
    console.log("Assigned ${newValue.toString(10)}");
  }
}
let c = new C();
c.p = c.p = 123;
c.p = 5;
// Not read, nor assigned what it doesn't take.
let wrong(): Void {
  c.p = "x";
  console.log(c.p.toString());
}
--- settled
(Block
  (Class
    ^C:0
    (Set
      ^p:4
      (Fn
